Hmm, `earlyConfDiags` doesn't include errors from backend initialization, so if I have a config that looks like this:

```
terraform {
  backend "local" {
    bad_attribute = "is bad"
  }
}

bad_block {

}
```

I won't see anything about the backend problems until after I fix any other config errors. 

That doesn't seem like a terrible outcome, but I wonder if it might be just as well to return all these diags together and either get rid of or adjust `errInitConfigError` so that it makes sense for both config errors and backend errors - the exact wording of that error message used to be important because `terraform-exec` relied on it, but that matching was since [removed](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-exec/pull/352).
